Content notes
- Classical texts (Judgments, Images and line statements) are from James Legge's
  translation, The Yi King (Sacred Books of the East, vol. 16, 1882), which is in
  the public domain. Source: Internet Sacred Text Archive (sacred-texts.com).
- The plain-English readings, Jungian commentary, history pages and all other
  original writing in this repository are released under the same MIT licence.
- No text from the Wilhelm/Baynes translation (still in copyright) is reproduced.
